<p>He will be able to do anything mentally (using the tulpa effect) and will experience extreme effects after. He can only use his ability from other Christians. He was given this ability from god (hence the Christianity). His dog will come after the effects as a defence and will emit a memetic effect converting anyone who views it to Christianity so the boy can still use his effect. More in pitch. (First time writing, already writ most of it asking off of reddit, sorry! I will post the draft later.)</p>
<p><em>I've trimmed your thread summary as it was very lengthy. Please keep it down to 1-3 lines to prevent taking up space on the forums. &#8212;RockTeethMothEyes</em></p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Religious History</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Get the fairly long containment procedure out the way then the SCP then his effects and SCP-xxxx-1A/B's effects, Discovery, His unique procedure , Interviews and maybe missions.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong>The SCP can do anything mentally with The Tulpa Effect, but only from Christian minds. This leads to fatigue and -1A will come. -1A is a big dog with supernatural features. When he comes, an effect known as -1B happens, -1B will make anyone viewing convert to Christianity. This is a fail safe for his ability.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> He can save the world if any K-Class end of the world scenario occurs. God gave the ability.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong>Descriptive word choices, depth in ability.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong>Human speech, Mission scenarios.</p>

